 long hair."], ["glasses", "los lentes / las gafas", 260, 360, "He wears glasses to read."], ["beard", "la barba", 420, 360, "My uncle has a beard."], ["bald", "calvo / calva", 580, 360, "The principal is bald."], ["strong", "fuerte", 740, 360, "She is strong; she carries the boxes."], ["thin", "delgado / delgada", 900, 360, "The runner is thin."]]}, {"id": "opposites", "n": 7, "title": "Opposites", "es": "Los opuestos", "scene": "opposites", "deck": "Learn them in pairs and you learn them twice as fast.", "words": [["big / small", "grande / pequeño", 90, 120, "The dog is big; the cat is small."], ["open / closed", "abierto / cerrado", 250, 120, "The store is open; the bank is closed."], ["full / empty", "lleno / vacío", 410, 120, "My cup is full; yours is empty."], ["clean / dirty", "limpio / sucio", 570, 120, "This shirt is clean; that one is dirty."], ["fast / slow", "rápido / lento", 730, 120, "The car is fast; the turtle is slow."], ["heavy / light", "pesado / ligero", 890, 120, "The box is heavy; the feather is light."], ["wet / dry", "mojado / seco", 90, 360, "My hair is wet; the towel is dry."], ["hot / cold", "caliente / frío", 250, 360, "The soup is hot; the ice is cold."], ["new / old", "nuevo / viejo", 410, 360, "The phone is new; the book is old."], ["loud / quiet", "ruidoso / silencioso", 570, 360, "The gym is loud; the library is quiet."], ["up / down", "arriba / abajo", 730, 360, "Go up the stairs and then down the hall."], ["same / different", "igual / diferente", 890, 360, "These are the same; those are different."]]}, {"id": "animals", "n": 8, "title": "Animals", "es": "Los animales", "scene": "animals", "deck": "Pets, farm, and the ones you meet in Mississippi whether you want to or not.", "words": [["dog", "el perro", 130, 180, "The dog sleeps by the door."], ["cat", "el gato", 330, 180, "The cat is on the roof."], ["bird", "el pájaro", 520, 150, "A red bird sits in the tree."], ["horse", "el caballo", 760, 170, "My uncle rides a horse."], ["rab